{
  "actors": [
    {
      "id": "bob",
      "label": "Bob",
      "role": "subject",
      "x": 82,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "api",
      "label": "Docs API",
      "role": "enforcer",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "authz",
      "label": "Authz service",
      "role": "decider",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "store",
      "label": "Tuple store",
      "role": "store",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 86
    },
    {
      "id": "cache",
      "label": "Decision cache",
      "role": "cache",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 14
    }
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "narration": "Bob (already authenticated) opens eng/plan. The Docs API knows the document id, so it must ask: may user:bob view doc:eng/plan? Default is deny.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "bob",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "GET eng/plan"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "authz",
          "label": "check viewer?"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "api": "deny by default"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "api"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The schema says viewer = direct viewers + editors + the parent folder's viewers. Nobody is listed directly on the document, so the walk reads its parent tuple (hop 1).",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "authz",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "doc:eng/plan#parent"
        },
        {
          "from": "store",
          "to": "authz",
          "label": "folder:eng"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "authz": "hop 1 of max 8"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "authz"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Folder eng is shared with a group, not a person: folder:eng#viewer@group:eng#member (hop 2).",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "authz",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "folder:eng#viewer"
        },
        {
          "from": "store",
          "to": "authz",
          "label": "group:eng#member"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "authz": "hop 2 of max 8"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "The last hop: group:eng#member@user:bob exists (hop 3). The path doc, folder, group, user proves bob is a viewer.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "authz",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "group:eng#member"
        },
        {
          "from": "store",
          "to": "authz",
          "label": "user:bob"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "authz": "ALLOW, 3 hops",
        "store": "3 reads"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "authz"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The decision returns to the API, which serves the document. It also caches the answer for 10 seconds so repeat opens skip the walk.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "authz",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "allow"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "cache",
          "label": "bob,eng/plan: allow 10s"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "bob",
          "label": "200 document"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "cache": "allow, ttl 10s"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "Later an admin removes bob from group eng: one tuple deleted, and every document under the folder closes at once. But the cached allow is still 6 seconds old.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "authz",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "delete bob member"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "store": "bob removed",
        "cache": "stale allow, 4s left"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "cache"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Bob reloads within the TTL and the cache still says allow. That is revocation lag: it is bounded by the TTL (10 s here), and you choose that number.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "bob",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "GET eng/plan"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "cache",
          "label": "lookup"
        },
        {
          "from": "cache",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "allow (stale)"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "api": "served from cache"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "cache"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "After the TTL the entry expires, the walk runs again, finds no path from user:bob to the document, and the default applies: deny, 403.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "authz",
          "label": "check viewer?"
        },
        {
          "from": "authz",
          "to": "api",
          "label": "deny, no path"
        },
        {
          "from": "api",
          "to": "bob",
          "label": "403"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "authz": "DENY",
        "cache": "expired"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "authz"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
